WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.934
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:10.176
Five years ago, I was sitting on
the couch in my mom's living room

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.970
when a Campbell's Soup
commercial caught my attention.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:18.790
Campbell's was releasing
its Star Wars branded soup.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:22.690
And a commercial began with
a dad feeding his little son

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.910
with Star Wars shaped
noodles in the spoon.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:33.615
Saying, and I quote,
Cooper, I am your father.

00:00:33.615 --> 00:00:38.020
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; The camera then zooms out, so

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.688
Cooper's second parent is also seen,
who then says emphatically,

00:00:42.688 --> 00:00:48.975
no Cooper, I am your father.

00:00:48.975 --> 00:00:53.559
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; My heart melts as

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:57.851
I quickly realize that without
singing word Campbell's was making

00:00:57.851 --> 00:01:02.380
a tremendous statement by choosing
to have two dads in its commercial.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:08.130
From that moment on I knew that
a company could sell products

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.480
while still taking a stand.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:16.140
Now five years ago, it had already been
three years since I'd first come out.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.618
But coming out is always
a continuous process.

00:01:18.618 --> 00:01:21.860
And I was slowly reconciling
the religious and

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:26.800
traditional views of my Caribbean
household with my own sexual orientation.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.770
While we've made tremendous
strides in representing

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.550
LGBT individuals in the media today,
they are still few and far between.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:41.250
A common belief is that brands should
stay out of social issues, and

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.360
many companies have chosen to stay
silent on issues going on today.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.700
This opinion is changing, however, and
consumer expectations are shifting.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.430
Instead, in a world where US consumers
state that they hold more trust

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:01.840
in businesses than in the government,
consumers are looking to businesses

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:06.200
to use their influence and their power
to make a difference in the world.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.740
And neutral is no longer neutral,
it's choosing to stay silent.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:19.310
In fact, according to Cohn Communications,
87% of consumers say they would

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.730
purchase a product because the company
supported an issue that they cared about.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.233
And 76% said they would refused to
purchase a product if a company held

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:33.390
views contrary to their beliefs.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:38.292
These statistics are evident in brands
that have gained support because of their

00:02:38.292 --> 00:02:42.617
social values, such as Everlean,
and brands that have lost support,

00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:49.252
such as Chick-Fil-A Prior
to my time at Stanford GSB,

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:54.174
I spent my career in marketing research
and strategy, digging into the mindsets of

00:02:54.174 --> 00:03:00.230
diverse consumers from all different age
groups, demographics, and backgrounds.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.710
I've interviewed hundreds of individuals.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:06.850
And one of the biggest learnings
that I've had is that individuals,

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.910
especially younger consumers,

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:13.490
are expecting businesses to be
more personal and more real.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.672
To showcase this, I'll share with
you an ad from the brand Always.

00:03:19.672 --> 00:03:21.768
&gt;&gt; Hi Erin.

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.435
[MUSIC]

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:25.739
Show me what it looks
like to run like a girl.

00:03:25.739 --> 00:03:27.627
[MUSIC]

00:03:27.627 --> 00:03:28.927
&gt;&gt; My freaking hair.

00:03:28.927 --> 00:03:31.679
[MUSIC]

00:03:31.679 --> 00:03:33.935
&gt;&gt; Show me what it looks
like to fight like a girl.

00:03:33.935 --> 00:03:38.830
&gt;&gt; [SOUND]
&gt;&gt; Now throw like a girl.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.092
[MUSIC]

00:03:40.092 --> 00:03:41.220
&gt;&gt; Awe.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:45.090
&gt;&gt; So do you think you
just insulted your sister?

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:49.100
&gt;&gt; No, I mean yeah,
insulted girls but not my sister.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.870
&gt;&gt; My name is Dakota,
and I'm ten years old.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.241
&gt;&gt; Show me what it looks
like to run like a girl.

00:03:56.241 --> 00:04:00.166
[MUSIC]

00:04:00.166 --> 00:04:01.424
Throw like a girl.

00:04:01.424 --> 00:04:02.829
[MUSIC]

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:03.913
Fight like a girl.

00:04:03.913 --> 00:04:08.050
[MUSIC]

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:11.995
What does it mean to you
when I say run like a girl?

00:04:11.995 --> 00:04:14.624
&gt;&gt; It means run fast as you can.

00:04:14.624 --> 00:04:20.468
[MUSIC]

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:24.604
&gt;&gt; This video has been viewed
over 90 million times,

00:04:24.604 --> 00:04:29.350
making it one of the most
watched ads of all time.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:33.250
This is incredible for an ad that
doesn't even showcase the product.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.025
And following the launch of the ad,

00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:39.860
Always' Twitter followers
tripled in three months.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.215
And in a study conducted, 70% of women and

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:49.070
60% of men said that the ad changed their
perception of the phrase like a girl.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.440
In the end,
it wasn't about the actual product,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.291
it was about what
the Always brand stood for.

00:04:56.291 --> 00:04:57.102
Since then,

00:04:57.102 --> 00:05:02.720
many other brands have followed suit
by choosing to join social movements.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:06.880
Starbucks, for example,
promised to hire 10,000

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.190
refugees following President Trump's
immigration ban in 2017.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:16.630
And following an incident in 2018,
where two black men were arrested for

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:21.000
using a Starbucks bathroom,
the company closed 8,000 retail

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.310
locations in order to hold racial bias
training for all of its employees.

00:05:26.756 --> 00:05:31.650
And lastly, following Nike's very
controversial Colin Kaepernick ad,

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:36.200
Fast Company reported that
Nike gained 163 million

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:41.070
in earned media and got a 31%
boost in sales the following week.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:44.990
In the end, it wasn't about the coffee or

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.470
the shoes,
it was about what these brands stood for.

00:05:48.605 --> 00:05:52.306
And actions like these will
become even more relevant,

00:05:52.306 --> 00:05:56.874
especially as consumer demands in
corporate social responsibility

00:05:56.874 --> 00:06:01.204
coincide with the fact that,
according to the US Census Bureau,

00:06:01.204 --> 00:06:05.241
50% of the US population
will be non-white by 2045.

00:06:05.241 --> 00:06:09.716
Now, I've often gotten the question,
how do we know if a brand

00:06:09.716 --> 00:06:13.530
is being authentic versus
just trying to make money?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:18.995
I've pondered this for a while with
the conclusion that I actually don't care.

00:06:18.995 --> 00:06:23.620
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Whether a brand is doing this

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:27.410
to sell more products or
to promote its social values,

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.820
if they do it well then the end
result is still the same.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.060
Nike will promote racial
justice in our country.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.380
Always will further the conversation
about gender equality.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:43.320
And Campbell's will normalize
LGBT relationships.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:45.457
And if they make money, even better.

00:06:48.018 --> 00:06:52.122
When I sit back and I reflect on
the Campbell Soup commercial today,

00:06:52.122 --> 00:06:55.720
I think about the power of representation.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.810
It's nearly impossible to
fathom what you can become

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.670
without seeing others who
have walked in your shoes.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:07.368
I personally remember the Campbell's Soup
commercial, so I can only imagine

00:07:07.368 --> 00:07:11.717
the countless other queer people that
the commercial impacted, perhaps

00:07:11.717 --> 00:07:16.368
individuals who grew up in much more
conservative environments than I was in.

00:07:16.368 --> 00:07:22.138
Or the power of the commercial on straight
individuals, helping to further normalize

00:07:22.138 --> 00:07:26.970
the fact that gay families exists and
are happy and are just like theirs.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:33.420
Moments like watching the Campbell Soup
commercial broadens perspectives,

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:37.640
it brings a sense of belonging,
and it can even change the world.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.270
So as future business leaders,
I'm asking that use your influence and

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.740
your power to promote change.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:50.802
The actions you take as advert as
having an ad promoting social issues,

00:07:50.802 --> 00:07:55.980
or as subtle as just having
diverse people in your ads,

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.030
do make a difference and can benefit
both your business and society.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.680
And lastly, we're all consumers.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:08.050
So I'm asking that you dig
internally to find the values

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.430
that are most important to you.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.810
For me it's diversity, where for
you it could be anything

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:17.990
from workers rights to public
health to the environment.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:22.670
Then I ask that you buy from companies
that do well in supporting those causes,

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:26.400
and that you stop buying from
companies that disappoint you.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:30.270
Then expect more,
expect that brands show up at protests,

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.210
that they pay employees fair wages, and

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:37.780
that the people who work there are as
diverse as the people they serve.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:43.208
The movement is growing, but
the movement depends on you.

00:08:43.208 --> 00:08:44.537
Thank you.

00:08:44.537 --> 00:08:46.009
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:08:46.009 --> 00:08:50.854
&gt;&gt; [MUSIC]

